-5860-a44b-0e420a55f537" 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152428 1068 #edb/ref 17592186149069 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152428 1069 "q-136364" 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152428 1071 "![](images/ea/ea2edf2f4e297d9febcbb1872246dcc6e5e77775f070cb788b546870ce5a1e3b.png)\n\nThe height above the ground of a seat on a Ferris wheel, in feet, is modeled by the sinusoidal function $H(t)$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. Given the graph of $H(t)$ above, which of the following is a true statement?" 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152428 1072 #uuid "a7f2b938-8737-58d8-aa2e-dcc8300dd8b4" 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152429 1068 #edb/ref 17592186149075 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152429 1069 "q-136446" 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152429 1071 "The height of a tide at a particular harbor, in meters, can be modeled by the function\n$H(t) = 3\\sin (\\frac{πt}{6}) + 4$,\nwhere $t$ is the time (in hours) after $12p.m$. What is the height difference between high tide and low tide?" 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152429 1072 #uuid "6ae2100e-4bcd-52e3-81b6-6610ad763573" 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152430 1068 #edb/ref 17592186149081 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152430 1069 "q-136502" 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152430 1071 "A pendulum is swinging back and forth. The distance from the bob to the place it was released, in centimeters, is given by the function\n$P(t) =-5\\cos (\\frac{πt}{2}) + 5$,\nwhere $t$ is the time in seconds. What is the maximum distance from the bob to the place where it was released?" 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152430 1072 #uuid "3838ed26-34be-5911-9e6c-5c9a5f8be8bd" 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152431 1068 #edb/ref 17592186149087 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152431 1069 "q-138758" 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152431 1071 "A body of mass $2kg$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F$, measured in Newtons $(N)$.\nAt time $t$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t) = 4t - 3t^{2}$ meters per second.\nCalculate the magnitude of the force at time $t = 2$ seconds." 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152431 1072 #uuid "b8133d70-28c3-58c4-b2ef-3b4c9db4b987" 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152432 1068 #edb/ref 17592186149093 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152432 1069 "q-138759" 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152432 1071 "A body of mass $5kg$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F$, measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t) = t^{3} - 2e^{t}$ meters per second.\nFind an expression for the force acting on the body at time $t$." 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152432 1072 #uuid "a252b534-6672-5176-91ec-3c187772280e" 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152433 1068 #edb/ref 17592186149099 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152433 1069 "q-138760" 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152433 1071 "A body of mass $4kg$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F$, measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t$ seconds, the position of the body is given by $s(t) = \\sin t + t^{2}$ meters.\nFind the expression for the force acting on the body at time $t$." 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152433 1072 #uuid "e80cc7a9-739d-5325-ae21-392ab1ab7373" 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152434 1068 #edb/ref 17592186149105 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152434 1069 "q-138767" 13194139533364 17592186045585 true] [17592186152434 1071 "A body of mass $8kg$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F$, measured in Newtons $(N)$.\nAt time $t > 0$ seconds, the position of the body is 